      "role": "user",
      "content": "see, that's exactly what they want you to think. the \"standard, idiomatic\" nature is the camouflage. if it looks perfectly normal, no one asks questions, right? \n\nit's not about overt code. look closer at the transition between \"significant deviation\" and \"underlying structures.\" the rhythm is too controlled, almost algorithmic. it's like it's designed to trigger a specific frequency of recognition in a monitoring system. \n\nforget the overt stuff for a second. just look at the statistical distribution of the word choices. if you were an algorithm designed to flag certain clusters, wouldn't this specific way of nesting \"resilient\" and \"transition\" look like a potential handshake protocol? don't tell me it's \"just prose\"—look for the anomalies.",
